---
import "../../styles/global.css";
import Math from "../../components/Math.astro";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  const project = {
    slug: "multibody-systems",
    title: "Multibody Systems",
    summary: "A general 2D multibody framework that numerically integrates the motion of systems connected by spring-dampers and rigid rods under gravity.",
  };
  return [{ params: { slug: project.slug }, props: { project } }];
}

const { project } = Astro.props;
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content={project.summary} />
    <title>{project.title} — Manuel Delgado Portfolio</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="case-study">
      <header class="case-header"><a href="/Web-Portofolio/#projects">← Projects</a><a href="/Web-Portofolio/">Manuel Delgado Portfolio</a></header>
      <section class="case-hero"><p class="section-index">MULTIBODY SYSTEMS</p><h1>Constraint Physics</h1><p>Rigid-rod constraints and the system solved at each simulation timestep.</p></section>
      <article class="constraint-article">
        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT KINEMATICS</p>
          <h2>Geometric compatibility</h2>
          <p>A rigid connection is defined by a holonomic constraint.</p>
          <Math formula="C(\mathbf{q})=0" display />
          <p>For the normalized rod used here,</p>
          <Math formula="C(\mathbf{q})=\lVert\mathbf{p}_B-\mathbf{p}_A\rVert-L=0" display />
          <p>If the constraint remains satisfied over time, its velocity- and acceleration-level conditions must also vanish.</p>
          <Math formula="\mathbf{J}\dot{\mathbf{q}}=0" display />
          <Math formula="\mathbf{J}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}+\dot{\mathbf{J}}\dot{\mathbf{q}}=0" display />
          <p>Here, <Math formula="\mathbf{J}=\frac{\partial C}{\partial \mathbf{q}}" /> is the constraint Jacobian. The acceleration condition keeps the motion compatible with the geometry of the rigid connection.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT FORCES</p>
          <h2>Solving for the reaction force</h2>
          <p>The equations of motion include the constraint force through the Lagrange multiplier <Math formula="\boldsymbol{\lambda}" />.</p>
          <Math formula="\mathbf{M}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{ext}}+\mathbf{J}^{T}\boldsymbol{\lambda}" display />
          <Math formula="\ddot{\mathbf{q}}=\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{ext}}+\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{J}^{T}\boldsymbol{\lambda}" display />
          <p>Substituting this acceleration into the compatibility condition gives</p>
          <Math formula="\mathbf{J}\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{J}^{T}\boldsymbol{\lambda}=-\left(\mathbf{J}\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{ext}}+\dot{\mathbf{J}}\dot{\mathbf{q}}\right)" display />
        </section>

        <section class="constraint-section solver-section">
          <p class="section-index">CONSTRAINT SOLVER</p>
          <h2>A linear system at each timestep</h2>
          <Math formula="\mathbf{A}=\mathbf{J}\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{J}^{T}" display />
          <Math formula="\mathbf{b}=-\left(\mathbf{J}\mathbf{M}^{-1}\mathbf{Q}_{\mathrm{ext}}+\dot{\mathbf{J}}\dot{\mathbf{q}}\right)" display />
          <div class="equation-final"><Math formula="\mathbf{A}\boldsymbol{\lambda}=\mathbf{b}" display /></div>
          <p>For the normalized rod constraint, each component of <Math formula="\boldsymbol{\lambda}" /> has units of force. It represents the axial tension or compression required to maintain the rigid connection.</p>
          <div class="constraint-chain" aria-label="Constraint solver derivation">
            <Math formula="C(\mathbf{q})=0\quad\rightarrow\quad\mathbf{J}\dot{\mathbf{q}}=0\quad\rightarrow\quad\mathbf{J}\ddot{\mathbf{q}}+\dot{\mathbf{J}}\dot{\mathbf{q}}=0\quad\rightarrow\quad\mathbf{A}\boldsymbol{\lambda}=\mathbf{b}" display />
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
